Example Dockerfile for a Java 17 Maven web application compatible with Tomcat 10:

```
FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-17 AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
RUN mvn clean package -DskipTests

FROM tomcat:10.1-jdk17
COPY --from=build /app/target/*.war /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/ROOT.war
EXPOSE 8080
```

For older `javax.servlet` applications, use a compatible Tomcat version such as Tomcat 9.

Build and run:

```
sudo docker build -t webapp .
sudo docker run -d --name app-demo -p 6060:8080 webapp
```

Allow **Custom TCP 6060** in the EC2 security group, then open:

```
http://PUBLIC_IP:6060
```

### **AWS troubleshooting**

| Problem                  | Check                                                   |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| SSH timed out            | Port 22, correct IPv4 source, public IP, subnet routing |
| Permission denied        | `.pem` key and Ubuntu username                          |
| Website not opening      | Security group port, container status, port mapping     |
| Docker permission denied | Use `sudo docker`                                       |
| Browser shows 404        | WAR filename/context path or app routes                 |
| Build failed             | Dockerfile, Maven errors, Java version                  |

